  "narrative": "The new validation materially changes one conditional conclusion and closes two response-deadline claims.\n\nFirst, H83 was the conditional test of feature_063=1 versus 0 within the feature_037=0 stratum, claimed in the stronger-dependency direction. The discovery result was signed +0.2383 [0.1396, 0.3371]. The independent validation result was signed +0.2694 [0.1285, 0.4104] under the stringent validation interval. Both point estimates are above the 0.15 composite dependency-score threshold, and both intervals exclude zero; the validation point is not attenuated relative to discovery. The lower confidence bounds fall just below the threshold, so the precise threshold margin remains uncertain. Nevertheless, the consistency and magnitude of the two independent estimates, including a replication under a stringent interval, support accepting H83 as a scientifically meaningful within-dataset association: feature_063 remains associated with stronger dependency when the large feature_037 signal is held at its comparator level. This should be interpreted as a conditional association and persistence evidence, not yet as formal effect modification. The complementary sparse stratum H84 and the registered feature_063-by-feature_037 interaction H86 remain the relevant follow-ups.\n\nSecond, the response deadline for H59 is unfavorable. H59 tested feature_003=1 versus 0 in the high-log-PFS eligibility stratum in the claimed stronger-dependency direction. Discovery was signed +0.1889 [0.0355, 0.3423], near and slightly above threshold in point estimate but wide. Independent validation was signed +0.1226 [-0.0656, 0.3109], below threshold and compatible with no effect even under the discovery-scale null. Because the validation did not reproduce a threshold-level association and the broader feature_003 line has been subthreshold or inconsistent, I reject H59 and close that conditional feature_003 line. This does not prove absence of a small effect; it means the threshold-level claim is not supported.\n\nThird, the response deadline for H40 confirms a null pattern for feature_001. Discovery was signed +0.0011 [-0.0762, 0.0783], and independent validation was signed -0.0127 [-0.1242, 0.0989], essentially flat in the claimed direction. I reject H40 and close it.\n\nOverall, the strongest within-dataset evidence now supports four measured binary predictors: feature_002=1 versus 0 with a large less-negative effect, feature_010=1 versus 0 with a less-negative effect, feature_037=1 versus 0 with a large stronger-dependency effect, and feature_063=1 versus 0 with a replicated stronger-dependency effect. The conditional panel indicates that feature_002, feature_010, and feature_037 persist when one another is fixed at a level, and feature_063 persists at least within the feature_002=1 and feature_010=0 strata, with the newly accepted feature_037=0 conditional providing additional independence evidence. These remain dataset-specific associations, not causal effects or biological-mechanism claims.\n\nThe next most informative analyses are the registered feature_063 interactions H85 and H86. They ask whether the apparent attenuation in the sparse feature_010=1 and feature_037=1 strata is formal effect modification rather than sparse-cell noise. I also reactivate the reciprocal feature_010-within-feature_037 and feature_002-within-feature_010 conditional claims H67-H70 and H75-H76 to complete the independence panel now that feature_063 robustness is largely resolved. Finally, I reactivate the categorical contrast H35-H36 for feature_054 level_001 versus level_003 as a useful broad exploration if analysis capacity allows. H82 and H84 remain active but tested; they should be reassessed alongside their corresponding interactions before deciding whether to close or reverse them. The voluntary validation budget remains six new requests for future iterations.",
  "research_notes": "Updated synthesis after validation deadlines.\n\nSupported threshold-level associations in the supplied dataset: feature_002=1 vs 0 less-negative +0.8315 [0.7658,0.8972] and robust strata; feature_010=1 vs 0 less-negative +0.4232 [0.3268,0.5195]; feature_037=1 vs 0 stronger-dependency signed +0.8325 [0.7667,0.8983]; feature_063=1 vs 0 stronger-dependency discovery +0.2268 and validation +0.2897. New accepted conditional: feature_063 within feature_037=0 signed +0.2383 [0.1396,0.3371] discovery and +0.2694 [0.1285,0.4104] validation; lower bounds slightly below threshold but replicated and zero-excluding, accepted as conditional within-dataset association. Previously accepted conditionals remain: f010 within f002=0/1 (H71,H72), f037 within f002=0/1 (H73,H74), f002 within f037=0/1 (H77,H78), f063 within f002=1 (H80) and f063 within f010=0 (H81). H79 f063 within f002=0 remains closed unresolved borderline (+0.2325 [0.1327,0.3323]) and not validated; do not upgrade unless independent replication or interaction evidence supports it.\n\nClosed negative/subthreshold lines: H39 global f003 rejected after validation +0.1354 [0.0220,0.2489] below threshold; H59 f003 in high log-PFS rejected after validation +0.1226 [-0.0656,0.3109]; H40 f001 rejected after validation -0.0127 [-0.1242,0.0989]. Other broad negative/null lines remain: f007/f058/f015 main and interactions, f024, f041, f011, f048, f023, f060, f033, f053 severity contrast, f046 level_002 vs level_001, f052 level_001 vs level_003, f061 level_001 vs level_002, and f002 interactions with high log-PFS or f046 level_001. f003 and f031 are not supported threshold-level.\n\nActive/tested but awaiting interaction context: H82 f063 within f010=1 +0.1020 [-0.1869,0.3909] sparse/unresolved; H84 f063 within f037=1 +0.1316 [-0.0597,0.3230] sparse/unresolved. Registered interactions to test formal attenuation: H85 f063 interaction with f010=1 vs complement (direction positive for attenuation) and H86 f063 interaction with f037=1 vs complement (direction positive for attenuation). Analyze should prioritize H85/H86.\n\nReactivated for next analysis: H67-H70 reciprocal f010 within f037 and f037 within f010; H75-H76 f002 within f010 strata; H35-H36 f054 level_001 vs level_003 broad categorical. Still deferred: signature extreme-stratum marker conditionals H13-H18, rare binary H24, and several low-priority interactions/conditional pairs. Validation budget: 6 voluntary validation requests remain; already validated H39,H40,H44,H59,H83. All accepted claims are associations in this dataset, not causal, mechanistic, or generalizable effects."
